{
 "experiment": "alarm_path",
 "date": "2026-11-19",
 "method": "Discrete-event twin (islab.core.sim). Per condition, 500 independent seeded trials (seeds 10000-10499): one detector event (smoke/leak/forced entry in rotation) at t=120-180 s; AlarmHub encodes AES-128 encrypted ADM-CID DC-09, sends through EgressGate (purpose=alarm) over a simulated WAN (latency U(0.05, 0.25) s each way, loss applied independently each direction to frames and ACKs) to a simulated MonitoringCentre that decodes, checks CRC/length/timestamp band (-40/+20 s), de-duplicates by (account, sequence, token, event) and ACKs. Hub retries the same sequence number with a fresh timestamp after an ACK timeout plus exponential backoff with jitter. Receipt latency = first centre receipt minus event time. Interop: real localhost sockets against pysiaalarm receivers (aio TCP, aio UDP = what Home Assistant uses, and sync TCP).",
 "params": {
  "trials_per_condition": 500,
  "hub": {
   "ack_timeout": 5.0,
   "backoff_base": 1.0,
