 "limitations": [
  "WAN model is i.i.d. loss + fixed outage windows; no bursty loss, no TCP connection setup/teardown, no NAT or cellular backup path.",
  "Monitoring centre is a simulation using our own decoder; the pysiaalarm matrix is the only independent check, and pysiaalarm is a home-automation receiver, not a certified alarm receiving centre (ARC) receiver.",
  "DC-09 standard text was not consulted (paywalled); framing follows pysiaalarm code and public descriptions. Certification-level conformance is NOT claimed.",
  "One alarm per trial; no queueing of many simultaneous alarms or sequence-number wrap under load.",
  "Heartbeats run every 60 s but are not retried; supervision timing was tested in unit tests, not in this experiment.",
  "Ack timeout/backoff values are our choices, not taken from the standard."
 ]
